# Workflow authoring

Use this guide for pull-request delivery profiles. Preserve an approved
local-only profile's manual hosted workflows; this checker deliberately rejects
manual-only workflows and is not its gate. Repository policy and existing
subscription authority still apply.

## Required CI rules

- Trigger on `pull_request` and `push` to `main` only. Never use
  `pull_request_target`. Leave workflow-level path filters unset so required
  checks are not left pending by a skipped workflow.
- Group concurrency by both `github.workflow` and `github.ref`, with
  `cancel-in-progress: true`.
- Detect changed paths once, then run each area only when its paths change.
  Keep the `hygiene` area unconditional. Give each area one unique, literal
  check name, `gate / <area>`; do not expand area jobs with matrices.
- Pin every action to a full 40-character commit SHA. Resolve the upstream
  revision and follow the software supply-chain scan procedure before adopting
  a new action or updating a pin; a SHA alone is not a safety assessment.
- Set workflow `permissions: {contents: read}`. Job overrides must be identical.
  Do not pass secrets, inherit secrets, bind environments, or expose credentials
  to fork PR code. Use checkout with `persist-credentials: false`.
- Use standard GitHub-hosted runners, never self-hosted runner labels or groups.

These implement the CI contract. See GitHub's [workflow syntax](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax)
for event, permission, job and concurrency semantics.

## Adapt and check

Start with `../templates/ci.yml`. Replace the example `code` area with the
repository's real areas and gate commands. Include their sources, tests,
dependency manifests, shared build configuration and workflow paths in the
inline filters. Add a matching `changes.outputs.<area>` and one dependent job
for every filter. Keep hygiene unconditional. `setup-pre-commit` owns the local
gate and hook setup; do not duplicate that procedure here.

The template reuses existing action pins. `dorny/paths-filter` runs with an
empty token and a full checkout to use git instead of the PR API, which would
need an additional permission. Its [documented git fallback](https://github.com/dorny/paths-filter#usage)
compares PRs with their base branch and main pushes with the preceding push.

Run `python3 <skill-dir>/scripts/check-workflows.py <workflow> [<workflow> ...]`
with installed PyYAML 6.x. Exit 0 means the declared structural rules pass;
exit 1 lists violations or unreadable/malformed YAML. No arguments exits 2.
The checker supports this explicit `changes`/inline-filter/area-job shape;
unsupported expressions, reusable workflows, local actions and matrices fail
closed. It does not execute workflows or inspect referenced actions or gate
scripts. Inspect actual area coverage and script behavior, and observe a real
PR and push run before claiming operational proof. Pinning does not establish
that an action is safe or that shell code cannot leak data.

## Hosted budget

Standard hosted runners are free on public repositories. The
`gh_private_minutes` budget is 2,000 included minutes per account per month on
GitHub Free for private repositories, shared across those repositories; account
plans and runner multipliers affect consumption. Verify current entitlement
and remaining usage in [GitHub Actions billing](https://docs.github.com/en/billing/concepts/product-billing/github-actions).
Keep paid overage at zero with a hard stop. On exhaustion, stop hosted runs,
retain local gate evidence and report hosted evidence unavailable. Never enable
paid overage without owner authority or label missing hosted evidence PASS.
name: CI
on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [main]
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: ci-${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
  changes:
    name: Detect changes
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    outputs:
      code: ${{ steps.filter.outputs.code }}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@93cb6efe18208431cddfb8368fd83d5badbf9bfd # v5.0.1
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0
          persist-credentials: false
      - uses: dorny/paths-filter@0e4a8c6effa4802afeda77dc8d303f8176d7dfad # v3
        id: filter
        with:
          # Git mode needs no pull-requests permission, including on forks.
          token: ''
          base: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.base_ref || github.ref }}
          filters: |
            code:
              - 'src/**'
              - 'tests/**'
              - 'tools/ci/**'
              - '.github/workflows/**'
  code:
    name: gate / code
    needs: changes
    if: ${{ needs.changes.outputs.code == 'true' }}
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@93cb6efe18208431cddfb8368fd83d5badbf9bfd # v5.0.1
        with:
          persist-credentials: false
      - run: bash tools/ci/gate.sh --area code
  hygiene:
    name: gate / hygiene
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@93cb6efe18208431cddfb8368fd83d5badbf9bfd # v5.0.1
        with:
          persist-credentials: false
      - run: bash tools/ci/gate.sh --area hygiene
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Check the documented PR workflow shape without executing any workflow code."""

import re
import sys
from pathlib import Path

import yaml


class WorkflowLoader(yaml.SafeLoader):
    """Keep Actions' `on` key a string and reject ambiguous duplicate keys."""

    yaml_implicit_resolvers = {
        key: [(tag, regex) for tag, regex in values if not tag.endswith(':bool')]
        for key, values in yaml.SafeLoader.yaml_implicit_resolvers.items()
    }

    def construct_mapping(self, node, deep=False):
        result = {}
        for key_node, value_node in node.value:
            key = self.construct_object(key_node, deep=deep)
            if not isinstance(key, str) or key in result:
                raise ValueError('mapping keys must be unique strings')
            result[key] = self.construct_object(value_node, deep=deep)
        return result


WorkflowLoader.add_implicit_resolver(
    'tag:yaml.org,2002:bool', re.compile(r'^(?:true|false)$'), list('tf')
)
RUNNERS = {'ubuntu-latest', 'ubuntu-24.04', 'ubuntu-22.04',
           'windows-latest', 'windows-2025', 'windows-2022',
           'macos-latest', 'macos-15', 'macos-14', 'ubuntu-24.04-arm'}
ACTION = re.compile(r'[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+/[A-Za-z0-9_./-]+@[0-9a-fA-F]{40}')
BASE = "${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.base_ref || github.ref }}"


def check(document):
    errors = []

    def require(condition, message):
        if not condition:
            errors.append(message)

    require(isinstance(document, dict), 'workflow must be a mapping')
    if errors:
        return errors
    events = document.get('on')
    require(events == {'pull_request': None, 'push': {'branches': ['main']}}
            or events == {'pull_request': {}, 'push': {'branches': ['main']}},
            'triggers: require pull_request and push branches [main] only')
    permissions = {'contents': 'read'}
    require(document.get('permissions') == permissions, 'permissions: contents: read only')
    concurrency = document.get('concurrency', {})
    require(isinstance(concurrency, dict)
            and concurrency.get('cancel-in-progress') is True
            and isinstance(concurrency.get('group'), str)
            and '${{ github.workflow }}' in concurrency['group']
            and '${{ github.ref }}' in concurrency['group'],
            'concurrency: workflow and ref group with cancel-in-progress true')
    # Reject secret references anywhere, including bracket notation and inherited secrets.
    require(not re.search(r'\bsecrets\b', str(document), re.I), 'secrets: forbidden in PR workflows')
    jobs = document.get('jobs')
    require(isinstance(jobs, dict) and bool(jobs), 'jobs: require area jobs')
    if not isinstance(jobs, dict):
        return errors
    filters = {}
    changes = jobs.get('changes', {})
    if isinstance(changes, dict):
        steps = changes.get('steps', [])
        if isinstance(steps, list) and len(steps) == 2 and all(isinstance(s, dict) for s in steps):
            checkout, filtering = steps
            require(str(checkout.get('uses', '')).startswith('actions/checkout@')
                    and checkout.get('with', {}).get('fetch-depth') == 0
                    and not (set(checkout) - {'uses', 'with', 'name'}),
                    'paths: changes must start with unconditional full checkout')
            inputs = filtering.get('with', {})
            require(str(filtering.get('uses', '')).startswith('dorny/paths-filter@')
                    and filtering.get('id') == 'filter'
                    and not (set(filtering) - {'uses', 'id', 'with', 'name'})
                    and isinstance(inputs, dict) and inputs.get('token') == ''
                    and inputs.get('base') == BASE
                    and not (set(inputs) - {'filters', 'token', 'base'}),
                    'paths: require unconditional filter with git fallback and event base')
            if isinstance(inputs, dict) and isinstance(inputs.get('filters'), str):
                filters = yaml.load(inputs['filters'], Loader=WorkflowLoader)
        else:
            require(False, 'paths: changes requires checkout and filter steps only')
        require(not (set(changes) & {'if', 'strategy', 'continue-on-error', 'env', 'defaults'}),
                'paths: changes must run unconditionally without overrides')
    require(isinstance(filters, dict) and bool(filters), 'paths: require inline area filters')
    if not isinstance(filters, dict):
        filters = {}
    for area, patterns in filters.items():
        require(re.fullmatch(r'[a-z][a-z0-9_]*', area) is not None
                and area not in {'changes', 'hygiene'}
                and isinstance(patterns, list) and bool(patterns)
                and all(isinstance(p, str) and bool(p) and not p.startswith('!') for p in patterns),
                'paths: area filters require named areas and positive path patterns')
    require(set(jobs) - {'changes', 'hygiene'} == set(filters),
            'paths: filters and area jobs must correspond exactly')
    expected_outputs = {area: '${{ steps.filter.outputs.' + area + ' }}' for area in filters}
    require(isinstance(changes, dict) and changes.get('outputs') == expected_outputs,
            'paths: changes outputs must come from the filter step')
    names = set()
    for area, job in jobs.items():
        require(isinstance(job, dict), f'{area}: job must be a mapping')
        if not isinstance(job, dict):
            continue
        runner = job.get('runs-on')
        require(isinstance(runner, str) and runner in RUNNERS,
                f'{area}: runners must be standard GitHub-hosted labels')
        require(job.get('permissions', permissions) == permissions,
                f'{area}: permissions override must be contents: read only')
        require(not (set(job) & {'uses', 'environment', 'strategy', 'container', 'services'}),
                f'{area}: unsupported reusable, environment, matrix or container job')
        name = job.get('name')
        require(isinstance(name, str) and bool(name) and '${{' not in name
                and name not in names and (area == 'changes' or name == f'gate / {area}'),
                f'{area}: check names must be stable and unique, gate / <area>')
        if isinstance(name, str):
            names.add(name)
        if area in filters:
            require(job.get('needs') in ('changes', ['changes'])
                    and job.get('if') == "${{ needs.changes.outputs." + area + " == 'true' }}",
                    f'{area}: paths condition must use its changes output')
        if area == 'hygiene':
            require('if' not in job and 'needs' not in job, 'hygiene must run unconditionally')
        steps = job.get('steps')
        require(isinstance(steps, list) and bool(steps), f'{area}: require steps')
        if not isinstance(steps, list):
            continue
        for step in steps:
            require(isinstance(step, dict), f'{area}: step must be a mapping')
            if not isinstance(step, dict):
                continue
            if 'uses' in step:
                action = step['uses']
                require(isinstance(action, str) and ACTION.fullmatch(action) is not None,
                        f'{area}: actions must use a full commit SHA')
                if isinstance(action, str) and action.startswith('actions/checkout@'):
                    require(isinstance(step.get('with'), dict)
                            and step['with'].get('persist-credentials') is False,
                            f'{area}: checkout must not persist credentials')
    return errors


def main(paths):
    if not paths:
        print('usage: check-workflows.py WORKFLOW [WORKFLOW ...]', file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    failed = False
    for path in paths:
        try:
            errors = check(yaml.load(Path(path).read_text(encoding='utf-8'), Loader=WorkflowLoader))
        except (OSError, UnicodeError, yaml.YAMLError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError, RecursionError):
            errors = ['unreadable, malformed or unsupported workflow structure']
        for error in errors:
            print(f'{path}: {error}', file=sys.stderr)
        if not errors:
            print(f'{path}: PASS')
        failed |= bool(errors)
    return int(failed)


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
"""AC-AFC-CI-02: exercise the real checker process with YAML workflow fixtures."""

from pathlib import Path
import subprocess
import sys

import pytest


SKILL = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
TEMPLATE = (SKILL / 'templates/ci.yml').read_text()
CHECKER = SKILL / 'scripts/check-workflows.py'


def invoke(*paths):
    return subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(CHECKER), *map(str, paths)],
                          capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)


def test_shipped_template_passes():
    result = invoke(SKILL / 'templates/ci.yml')
    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr
    assert 'PASS' in result.stdout


@pytest.mark.parametrize(('before', 'after', 'diagnostic'), [
    ('pull_request:', 'pull_request_target:', 'triggers'),
    ('branches: [main]', 'branches: [other]', 'triggers'),
    ('  push:', '  workflow_dispatch:\n  push:', 'triggers'),
    ('${{ github.ref }}', 'fixed', 'concurrency'),
    ('cancel-in-progress: true', 'cancel-in-progress: false', 'concurrency'),
    ("${{ needs.changes.outputs.code == 'true' }}", 'true', 'paths condition'),
    ("${{ needs.changes.outputs.code == 'true' }}", "${{ needs.changes.outputs.code == 'true' || true }}", 'paths condition'),
    ('${{ steps.filter.outputs.code }}', "${{ 'true' }}", 'outputs'),
    ('needs: changes', 'needs: other', 'paths condition'),
    ("token: ''", 'token: ${{ github.token }}', 'git fallback'),
    ('fetch-depth: 0', 'fetch-depth: 1', 'full checkout'),
    ('gate / code', 'gate / ${{ github.ref }}', 'stable'),
    ('gate / code', 'gate / hygiene', 'stable'),
    ('    name: gate / code', '    strategy:\n      matrix: {version: [1, 2]}\n    name: gate / code', 'matrix'),
    ('actions/checkout@93cb6efe18208431cddfb8368fd83d5badbf9bfd', 'actions/checkout@v5', 'full commit SHA'),
    ('dorny/paths-filter@0e4a8c6effa4802afeda77dc8d303f8176d7dfad', 'dorny/paths-filter@v3', 'full commit SHA'),
    ('contents: read', 'contents: write', 'permissions'),
    ('    name: gate / code', '    permissions: {contents: write}\n    name: gate / code', 'permissions'),
    ('bash tools/ci/gate.sh --area code', 'echo ${{ secrets.TOKEN }}', 'secrets'),
    ('bash tools/ci/gate.sh --area code', "echo ${{ secrets['TOKEN'] }}", 'secrets'),
    ('persist-credentials: false', 'persist-credentials: true', 'persist credentials'),
    ('ubuntu-latest', 'self-hosted', 'runners'),
    ('ubuntu-latest', 'ubuntu-custom-host', 'runners'),
    ('    name: gate / code', '    environment: production\n    name: gate / code', 'environment'),
    ('    name: gate / hygiene', '    if: false\n    name: gate / hygiene', 'unconditionally'),
], ids=['target-event', 'push-branch', 'extra-event', 'concurrency-ref', 'cancel',
        'area-unconditional', 'condition-bypass', 'output-bypass', 'dependency',
        'filter-token', 'shallow-checkout', 'dynamic-name', 'duplicate-name', 'matrix',
        'checkout-tag', 'filter-tag', 'workflow-write', 'job-write', 'secret-dot',
        'secret-bracket', 'persist-token', 'self-hosted', 'custom-runner',
        'environment', 'conditional-hygiene'])
def test_rule_violation_exits_one(tmp_path, before, after, diagnostic):
    assert before in TEMPLATE
    workflow = tmp_path / 'violating.yml'
    workflow.write_text(TEMPLATE.replace(before, after))
    result = invoke(workflow)
    assert result.returncode == 1, result.stdout + result.stderr
    assert diagnostic in result.stderr


@pytest.mark.parametrize('content', ['', 'jobs: [', 'jobs: []', 'jobs: {}\njobs: {}',
                                      '[]', 'on: push\njobs: {changes: null}'])
def test_malformed_workflow_fails_closed(tmp_path, content):
    path = tmp_path / 'malformed.yml'
    path.write_text(content)
    result = invoke(path)
    assert result.returncode == 1
    assert 'Traceback' not in result.stderr


def test_missing_file_and_multiple_workflows_fail(tmp_path):
    result = invoke(SKILL / 'templates/ci.yml', tmp_path / 'missing.yml')
    assert result.returncode == 1
    assert 'PASS' in result.stdout
    assert 'unreadable' in result.stderr


def test_missing_arguments_is_usage_error():
    assert invoke().returncode == 2
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Validate the skill and check independent forward-test classifications.

Set RELEASE_TRIGGER_RESULTS to the evaluator's JSON (case id -> MATCH/NO_MATCH).
Give the evaluator SKILL.md and trigger-requests.json without this checker.
"""

import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import unittest

import yaml


SKILL = Path(os.environ.get("RELEASE_SKILL_DIR", Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]))
CREATOR = Path.home() / ".codex/skills/.system/skill-creator/scripts/quick_validate.py"


class ReleaseProcessTests(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_creator_validation_and_repository_metadata(self):
        text = (SKILL / "SKILL.md").read_text()
        self.assertLess(len(text.splitlines()), 60)
        self.assertLess(len(text.split()), 400)
        _, header, body = text.split("---", 2)
        metadata = yaml.safe_load(header)
        self.assertEqual(metadata["name"], "release-process")
        for field in ("type", "title", "okf_status", "tags"):
            self.assertTrue(metadata[field], field)
        # The installed validator rejects HQ metadata. Validate its portable
        # fields unchanged; BRAN validates the complete repository document.
        portable = {key: value for key, value in metadata.items() if key in
                    {"name", "description", "license", "allowed-tools", "metadata"}}
        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as target:
            Path(target, "SKILL.md").write_text(
                "---\n" + yaml.safe_dump(portable) + "---" + body)
            subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(CREATOR), target], check=True)

    def test_trigger_classifications(self):
        requests = json.loads((Path(__file__).parent / "trigger-requests.json").read_text())
        results = json.loads(Path(os.environ["RELEASE_TRIGGER_RESULTS"]).read_text())
        self.assertEqual(set(results), set(requests))
        self.assertEqual(results, {"request_1": "MATCH", "request_2": "NO_MATCH"})


if __name__ == "__main__":
    unittest.main()
